From 4121f4e7576d6aa88c17738f1144d0a37fbcb670 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garv <garvagnihotri22@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(statusbar): add the Report Issue button

- port of the old fork's reportIssueStatusBar.ts: a "$(bug) Report Issue" entry on the left of the status bar,
  just before the problems indicator, that opens the issue tracker.
- it opens product.json's reportIssueUrl (https://github.com/loophole-ai/loophole-ide/issues/new as fallback).
- the address is opened directly in the browser: it comes from product.json and not from content the person
  opened, so the "Do you want Loophole to open the external website?" prompt would only get in the way.
- plain workbench contribution, the old fork's extra singleton service is not needed.
- only registered in the desktop build (workbench.desktop.main.ts).
---
 .../reportIssue.contribution.ts               | 51 +++++++++++++++++++
 src/vs/workbench/workbench.desktop.main.ts    |  3 ++
 2 files changed, 54 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/vs/workbench/contrib/loopholeReportIssue/electron-browser/reportIssue.contribution.ts

diff --git a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/loopholeReportIssue/electron-browser/reportIssue.contribution.ts b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/loopholeReportIssue/electron-browser/reportIssue.contribution.ts
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..f1148c68
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/loopholeReportIssue/electron-browser/reportIssue.contribution.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
